{"test":"oldpc-desktop","checks":["Archive remains available through the existing UI.","The archive query accepts keyboard focus.","Focused input keeps its readable paper instead of a dark overlay.","Focused archive buttons keep the same readable background.","Desktop shortcuts have drawn pictograms and readable captions over the wallpaper.","Start opens its application menu and gives its first entry keyboard focus.","Start menu remains inside the desktop.","Escape closes Start before leaving the computer and returns keyboard focus.","Opening a site index does not read its articles.","Desktop navigation must not grant investigation knowledge.","Typing the locked record ID cannot bypass its source conditions.","Denied source titles cannot leak into the address bar.","Denied browser page does not expose a locked title.","The browser opens a compiled local article through shared runtime.","The browser displays a readable local URL without a content ID.","Article text uses a readable 24 design-pixel baseline at 720p.","A real page link reaches another compiled source.","The actual read article contains authored internal links, so the paper check exercises real content.","The browser reached this source through its real link without automatically recording it.","The read article offers the visible manual \u0412 \u043A\u043D\u0438\u0436\u043A\u0443 action.","The ordinary browser save action completed through the shared runtime.","The linked article has exactly one stored source entry, including after the existing slot reload.","The selected paper source preserves both visible link labels without exposing machine destinations.","Recording and displaying the already read linked source creates no additional knowledge.","Closing the paper source releases its existing journal screen.","The social site uses its visible feed rather than the article pane.","Visible social cards render the authored post and reply authors.","Replies have distinct comment cards inside the same source.","A social card preserves the locked family-photo gate without exposing its title.","Source-link punctuation is never mistaken for an author label or shown as an internal address.","The first profile link remains complete and visibly underlined.","The formerly broken first profile link opens Alsu through the shared runtime.","A resident profile has its own identity card without inventing a portrait.","All currently visible social bodies follow the 1.6 text-scale setting.","Large text keeps browser controls inside the desktop.","Large text keeps the taskbar inside the desktop.","Large desktop captions fit their longest word without breaking it into fragments.","Desktop captions keep a dark outline over the snow in the wallpaper.","Large desktop shortcuts stay inside the screen.","Large desktop shortcut stays inside the actual screen: Icon_files","Large desktop glyph stays inside its actual shortcut: Icon_files","Large desktop glyph stays inside the actual screen: Icon_files","Large desktop shortcut stays inside the actual screen: Icon_archive","Large desktop glyph stays inside its actual shortcut: Icon_archive","Large desktop glyph stays inside the actual screen: Icon_archive","Large desktop shortcut stays inside the actual screen: Icon_browser","Large desktop glyph stays inside its actual shortcut: Icon_browser","Large desktop glyph stays inside the actual screen: Icon_browser","Large desktop shortcut stays inside the actual screen: Icon_pictures","Large desktop glyph stays inside its actual shortcut: Icon_pictures","Large desktop glyph stays inside the actual screen: Icon_pictures","Large desktop shortcut stays inside the actual screen: Icon_notepad","Large desktop glyph stays inside its actual shortcut: Icon_notepad","Large desktop glyph stays inside the actual screen: Icon_notepad","Large desktop shortcut stays inside the actual screen: Icon_trash","Large desktop glyph stays inside its actual shortcut: Icon_trash","Large desktop glyph stays inside the actual screen: Icon_trash","History clears the previous social feed before rendering navigation.","Returning to TatWiki restores the article reader without stale social cards.","Personal note keeps Tatar characters.","Activating the browser moves keyboard input out of the background note.","Alt\u002BTab returns keyboard input to the foreground note.","Window-title appearance follows the application that receives keyboard input.","Delete moves the personal note into the simulated recycle bin.","File manager refits after large-text settings and folder changes.","The file-manager status remains above the taskbar.","Recycle-bin restore returns the same stable personal file.","Text editor renders the formatted page.","Dragging the title updates a clamped window position.","Minimize hides only the selected application.","Taskbar restores and focuses the application.","Taskbar restoration also restores keyboard focus to the browser.","The existing game slot stores desktop state.","A separate fresh session starts normally.","New game does not inherit another session\u0027s notes.","The existing save loader restores the desktop capability.","Load restores both personal files and the recycle-bin consequence.","Browser history survives the shared save.","Restored history presents a local URL while preserving stable source IDs.","Open windows survive the shared save.","Reopening the saved desktop focuses its foreground application.","The actual read article contains authored internal links, so the paper check exercises real content.","The linked article has exactly one stored source entry, including after the existing slot reload.","The selected paper source preserves both visible link labels without exposing machine destinations.","Recording and displaying the already read linked source creates no additional knowledge.","Closing the paper source releases its existing journal screen.","The personal photograph remains gated before reading its original arrival source.","A typed photograph URL cannot reveal the unread personal source.","Browsing the picture list neither exposes the gated photograph nor grants its memory.","The existing arrival photograph is the available source of the personal memory.","Reading the actual arrival document unlocks its saved photograph through ordinary source effects.","The original photograph reader closes before opening the desktop.","The picture application displays the real saved family photograph.","The picture\u0027s Text tab preserves the visible source link without exposing its technical destination.","The actual picture-source link opens its existing related document in the browser.","Viewing the copy and following its household link grants no extra knowledge, words, journal entries or locked investigation access."],"status":"pass","visual":"captured-if-requested"}
